# A directory whose chain loops (roadmap os-server.md P15, the second
# review; tests/posix/edges.c, EDGES_LOOP): B:\MANY's first cluster, whose
# 32 entries are all used, links to itself. A lookup, a create and a
# listing there are EIO after one walk along the chain, as long as the
# volume has clusters (before, a walk from the start for each entry: 464
# seconds of Bochs for one lookup, the server's lock held).
program: idle
define: TEST_POSIX_EDGES
define: EDGES_LOOP
media: B loop
keys: {wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}{wait 250}
match: contains
timeout: 120
emulators: bochs
---
edges: a name in a directory whose chain loops (-1, EIO 5): -1, errno 5
edges: a file made there (-1, EIO 5): -1, errno 5
edges: its listing ends, EIO (1 5): 1 5
edges: done
